- # `↯/s.101.1` — `Bind.Error`
+ # `↯/s.101.1` — `Bind.Error`

- Raised when Coaxial cannot bind a socket.
+ Se lanza cuando Coaxial no puede ligar un socket.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- The OS refused to allocate the requested socket. The constructor
- takes a `reason: Reason`; the rendered message is `the socket
+ El sistema operativo se negó a asignar el socket solicitado. El constructor toma un
+ `reason: Reason`; el mensaje representado es `the socket

- could not be bound because $reason`.
+ could not be bound because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.101.1.1` — `PortInUse`
+ ### `↯/s.101.1.1` — `PortInUse`

- Another process is already bound to the requested port.
+ Otro proceso ya está ligado al puerto solicitado.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.101.1.1] the socket could not be bound because another process is already bound to the port`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.101.1.1] the socket could not be bound because another process is already bound to the port`

- **Resolution.** Free the port (stop the conflicting process) or
- choose a different port.
+ **Solución.** Libera el puerto (detén el proceso en conflicto) o elige otro puerto.

- ### `↯/s.101.1.2` — `PermissionDenied`
+ ### `↯/s.101.1.2` — `PermissionDenied`

- The current user does not have permission to bind the requested
- port — typically the case for ports below 1024 on POSIX systems.
+ El usuario actual no tiene permiso para ligar el puerto solicitado, lo que suele ocurrir con los
+ puertos por debajo de 1024 en los sistemas POSIX.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.101.1.2] the socket could not be bound because the user does not have permission to bind the port`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.101.1.2] the socket could not be bound because the user does not have permission to bind the port`

- **Resolution.** Run with elevated privileges, or choose an
- unprivileged port.
+ **Solución.** Ejecuta con privilegios elevados, o elige un puerto sin privilegios.

- ### `↯/s.101.1.3` — `AddressUnavailable`
+ ### `↯/s.101.1.3` — `AddressUnavailable`

- The requested address is not available on this host (e.g. binding
- to an IP that no interface owns).
+ La dirección solicitada no está disponible en este anfitrión (por ejemplo, al ligar a una IP que
+ no pertenece a ninguna interfaz).

- **Example.** `[↯/s.101.1.3] the socket could not be bound because the requested address is not available on this host`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.101.1.3] the socket could not be bound because the requested address is not available on this host`

- **Resolution.** Verify the address is configured on a local
- interface, or bind to `0.0.0.0` / `::` for any interface.
+ **Solución.** Comprueba que la dirección está configurada en una interfaz local, o liga a
+ `0.0.0.0` / `::` para cualquier interfaz.

